# seed-linux.hex - asm0, the seed assembler, for x86-64 Linux, as commented
# hexadecimal (PLAN D67). Made from bootstrap/seed/asm0-linux.eas by mkhex.py.
#
# A comment runs from # to the end of the line; everything else is pairs of hex
# digits, the bytes of the program in order. Each line starts with the bytes of
# one statement; the comment gives its file offset and source. Turn it into the
# program with the OS alone:
#     sh hex2bin.sh seed-linux.hex asm0          (POSIX sh, awk, printf)
#     .\hex2bin.ps1 seed-linux.hex asm0.exe     (PowerShell)
# CI checks that this asm0 assembles asm0-linux.eas to exactly these bytes, and
# Stage 0 to exactly the bytes NASM gives.

